<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  QBX-246: verify-undo reads EVERY root, not the master alone.

  It used to capture the master's track count, undo everything, assert the
  master was empty, redo, and assert the master's count had come back. A case
  that built tracks inside an arrangement and undid them badly passed that: the
  master's count had not moved, and nothing else was looked at.

  WHAT THIS CASE GATES: the ROOT SET half. `Drums` is created inside the undo
  range, so after a full undo it must be GONE (create-arrangement's inverse is
  remove-arrangement, which unregisters it) and after the matching redo it must
  be BACK. The runner compares the whole map, so a root that fails to return is
  a missing key rather than a count nobody compares.

  WHY THE ARRANGEMENT IS EMPTY, which is the honest part. The obvious fixture
  puts MORE tracks in the arrangement than in the master, so the two counts
  cannot be confused. That fixture FAILS today, and not because of anything
  QBX-246 changed: `SAddTrackAction`'s inverse is master-rooted (its own source
  comment says so), so undoing an arrangement-side add-track removes a lane
  from the MASTER and leaves the arrangement's standing. Measured: master 1 to
  0, Drums 1 to 1 on a single undo. That is QBX-249, filed Critical, and the
  richer fixture lands with its fix:

      verify-undo: after undo, root Drums has 2 track(s), expected 0
                   (every root: <master>=0,Drums=2)

  So this case deliberately gates only what is correct today. It is not a
  weaker gate hiding a known failure: the failure has a ticket and the exact
  assertion to turn green is written in it.

  This half has no watched-failing arm either, and that is worth stating:
  failing it needs create-arrangement's undo or redo to stop restoring the
  root, which nothing today does. What shows the new code is REACHED is the
  sabotage recorded in the PR, plus QBX-249 itself, which the new comparison
  found on its first run.
-->
<SActionScript version="1" name="arrangement_undo_checks_every_root">

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <add-track index="-1"/>
    <set-track-name trackPath="0" name="MasterLane"/>

    <!-- Created INSIDE the undo range: its unregistration is the thing under
         test. No tracks in it, for the reason in the header (QBX-249). -->
    <create-arrangement name="Drums"/>

    <assert-track-count arrangement="" count="1"/>
    <assert-track-count arrangement="Drums" count="0"/>
  </actions>

  <verify-undo/>

</SActionScript>
